<h3>1.5 A worked step for the kill-switch arm</h3>
<p>The kill-switch arm scores the same visits with the same key counts. At the step of Figure 1 the CPU arm scores 17 full pages plus 15 keys; with the kernel disabled that is 17 avx_full_page visits of 64 keys plus one AVX visit of 15 keys. The AoF arm is unchanged by the kill switch: the card still scores 1,100 keys and the CPU 3.</p>

<h2>2. Section "5. Token jobs by path set"</h2>

<div class="q">Q: rephrase "How many token jobs of a class touched which paths within a forward (a job may use several paths across its pages and layers)" in plain English.</div>
<p>Replacement text for the section intro:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A token job is one token of one user inside one forward. During that forward the token's keys are scored layer by layer, KV head by KV head, page by page, and each (KV head, page) step takes one path: the AMX kernel, the AVX loop or the FPGA card. One token job therefore usually touches more than one path in a forward, for example the kernel for its full pages and the AVX loop for its pending page.</p>
<p>The table counts token jobs by the combination of paths that touched them. Each token job goes into exactly one column: the set of all paths it used in its forward, over all layers, KV heads and pages. The counts add up over every forward of the class.</p>
</blockquote>

<div class="q">Q: the sentence says "within a forward", but the forwards column shows 256, 64, etc. How do they correlate?</div>
<p>"Within a forward" describes how one token job is classified: its path set is collected over the one forward it belongs to, then it is counted once. The counts in the row are then summed over all forwards of the class. So:</p>
<ul>
<li>token jobs = sum over the forwards of the class of the token jobs in each forward. Decode for qwen: 255 forwards x 8 users = 2,040 token jobs. Prompt 1024 prefill: 8 forwards x 1,024 jobs (8 users x a 128-token chunk) = 8,192. Prompt 8192 prefill: 64 forwards x 1,024 = 65,536.</li>
<li>the eight path-set columns of a row add up to the token jobs column. qwen CPU decode amxon: 24 (amx only) + 2,016 (avx+amx) = 2,040.</li>
<li>a per-forward view is the row divided by the forwards: qwen CPU decode amxon has 8 token jobs per forward; in 3 of the 255 forwards all 8 jobs are "amx" only (the page-completing steps), in the other 252 all 8 are "avx+amx".</li>
</ul>
